  "text": "Melor, also called St. Melor, is a saint of Cornwall and Brittany. He was a priest of the early medieval age. In one account he was the son of a Breton prince. The brother of his father had him maimed and then beheaded. As the killer carried off the head, it began to speak. Melor told him to strike the ground with his staff. Clear water rushed out, and the staff took root and grew into a flowering tree. Healing wells in the forest were named for Melor. His great shrine stood at Lanmeur, and there are sanctuaries also at Linkinhorne in Cornwall. At these wells the sick came to be healed. Melor seems to have taken the place of an older god or goddess of healing, so the old ways could live on under the new faith.",
